  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "McGonigle et al. Metabolic Potential of Microbial Communities in the Hypersaline Sediments of the Bonneville Salt Flats. mSystems (2022). DOI: 10.1128/msystems.00846-22. [PMC9765009]",
  "doi": "10.1128/msystems.00846-22",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9765009/",
  "notes": "Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: All of the saltwater media were adapted from the Halohandbook (60), contained NaCl, MgCl2·6H2O, MgSO4·7H2O, KCl, TrisHCl, and included B vitamins (thiamine and biotin) as well as the following trace e). Component names mapped to BiGG (see mapping_confidence); presence-based bounds unless the paper gave exchange bounds; concentration_mM where units allowed. Extraction confidence: low.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "verification_evidence": "All of the saltwater media were adapted from the Halohandbook (60), contained NaCl, MgCl2·6 H2O, MgSO4·7 H2O, KCl, TrisHCl, and included B vitamins (thiamine and biotin) as well as the following trace elements: MnCl2·4 H2O, ZnSO4·7 H2O, FeSO4·7 H2O, and CuSO4·5 H2O ... amended with one of the following: bicarbonate, glucose, or acetate, each at 0.07 M.",
  "verification_confidence": "medium",
